# Architecture

## Product
- **PayDefteri** — multi-partner installment tracker for Turkish savings-finance plans (and similar shared payment plans).
- Audience: co-buyer / household SaaS — not financing-company back-office.
- Functional spec: `fuzul-taksit-takip.html` (localStorage prototype). Preserve behavior; harden for multi-plan + auth.
- “Fuzul” appears only as an optional seed template, not the product brand.
- **Sharing:** Plan owner invites paydaş by email → member linked to a Partner; each user may mark **only their own** partner payments.

## Stack
- Frontend: Angular standalone + signals → `src/web`
- Backend: ASP.NET Core Web API, Clean Architecture → `src/api`
- DB: PostgreSQL + EF Core
- Auth: JWT; plan-level authorization

## Bounded context (Installment Tracking)
| Entity | Role |
|--------|------|
| Plan | `title`, `desc`, `deliveryInstId` |
| Partner | `name`, `color`, `defaultPct` |
| Installment | `name`, `dueDate`, `totalAmount`, `shareType` |
| Payment | per partner: paid, paidAt, paidByPartnerId, note |
| Settlement | derived from pay-on-behalf (`paidBy ≠ owner`) |

Share types: `default` | `equal` | `custom`. Status: `pending` | `partial` | `full`.

## Layout
```
src/api/{Domain,Application,Infrastructure,Api}
src/web/src/app/{core,shared,features/{dashboard,setup,data}}
tests/
```

## Rules
- Domain logic lives in .NET Domain/Application — not Angular templates.
- One plan owns many partners and installments; users may own many plans.
- Prefer small PRs; ADR for cross-cutting decisions.
- Do not invent CRM/Customer/Contract entities unless product scope expands.
